{"type":"event","event":{"type":"message_update","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"No taste file actually exists (the prompt showed a stub). Fine. Simple repo: just scheduler.py and test_public.py.\n\nNow implement Kahn's algorithm with a min-heap:\n\nRequirements recap:\n1. Topologically order all nodes → Kahn.\n2. Lexicographically smallest ready node each step → min-heap.\n3. ValueError for cycles.\n4. KeyError for deps absent from graph.\n5. Do not mutate input.\n\nEdge cases:\n- Empty graph → [].\n- deps given as lists, tuples, sets — iterating works.\n- Duplicate deps: dedupe per-node.\n- Self-dependency: cycle → ValueError.\n- Non-string keys: heap comparison may TypeError for mixed types; that's inherent. For homogeneous ints/strings it works.\n\nAlso should I handle `graph` being a mapping-like? `graph.items()` works for dicts; validate deps iterables implicitly.\n\nWrite the implementation:\n\n```python\nimport heapq\n\n\ndef schedule(graph):\n    dependencies = {}\n    for node, deps in graph.items():\n        seen = set()\n        for dep in deps:\n            if dep not in graph:\n                raise KeyError(dep)\n            seen.add(dep)\n        dependencies[node] = seen\n\n    indegree = {node: len(deps) for node, deps in dependencies.items()}\n    dependents = {node: [] for node in graph}\n    for node, deps in dependencies.items():\n        for dep in deps:\n            dependents[dep].append(node)\n\n    ready = [node for node, degree in indegree.items() if degree == 0]\n    heapq.heapify(ready)\n    out = []\n    while ready:\n        node = heapq.heappop(ready)\n        out.append(node)\n        for dependent in dependents[node]:\n            indegree[dependent] -= 1\n            if indegree[dependent] == 0:\n                heapq.heappush(ready, dependent)\n\n    if len(out) != len(graph):\n        raise ValueError(\"graph contains a cycle\")\n    return out\n```\n\nWait — memory: dependencies dict stores deduped sets; fine.\n\nOne 