{"type":"event","event":{"type":"message_update","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now let me verify with the public test and a set of additional checks. I'll write a temporary verification script... but rule says don't create evaluator-bypass files. A temp test file outside the repo (e.g., /tmp) is fine, then delete it. Or run python -c inline. Let me run the public test first, then a thorough inline check.\n\nI'll run the public test plus an inline stress test comparing against a brute-force reference for random DAGs, checking non-mutation, cycle detection, KeyError, empty graph, duplicates, self-loop, and lexicographic behavior.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Now I'll verify with the public test plus a thorough inline check covering lexicographic order, cycles, missing deps, non-mutation, and randomized DAGs against a brute-force reference."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"[CALL_00064]","name":"shell_command","input":{"command":"python3 test_public.py && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport copy, itertools, random\nfrom scheduler import schedule\n\n# basic lexicographic selection regardless of insertion order\nassert schedule({'b': ['a'], 'a': []}) == ['a', 'b']\nassert schedule({'c': ['a'], 'b': [], 'a': []}) == ['a', 'b', 'c']\nassert schedule({'c': ['a', 'b'], 'b': ['a'], 'a': []}) == ['a', 'b', 'c']\n# ties: only-ready nodes considered each step\nassert schedule({'z': [], 'a': ['y'], 'y': [], 'b': []}) == ['b', 'z', 'y', 'a'] or True\n# empty graph\nassert schedule({}) == []\n# independent nodes sorted\nassert schedule({'d': [], 'c': [], 'b': [], 'a': []}) == ['a', 'b', 'c', 'd']\n# duplicate and set deps handled idempotently\nassert schedule({'a': ['b', 'b'], 'b': []}) == ['b', 'a']\nassert schedule({'a': {'b'}, 'b': []}) == ['b', 'a']\n# cycle -> ValueError\nfor cyc in [{'a': ['b'], 'b': ['a']}, {'a': ['a']}, {'a': ['b'], 'b': ['c'], 'c': ['a'], 'd': []}]:\n    try:\n        schedule(cyc)\n        raise AssertionError('expected ValueError for %r' % (cyc,))\n    except ValueError:\n        pass\n# missing dep -> KeyError carrying the missing node\nfor bad in [{'a': ['x']}, {'a': [], 'b': ['a', 'missing']}]:\n    try:\n        schedule(bad)\n        raise AssertionError('expected KeyError for %r' % (bad,))\n    except KeyError as e:\n        assert e.args[0] == 'missing' or e.args[0] == 'x', e\n# KeyError takes precedence over cycle when both present\ntry:\n    schedule({'a': ['b'], 'b': ['a'], 'c': ['nope']})\n    raise AssertionError('expected KeyError')\nexcept KeyError:\n    pass\n# non-mutation\ng = {'c': ['a', 'b'], 'b': ['a'], 'a': []}\nsnap = copy.deepcopy(g)\nschedule(g)\nassert g == snap, g\n\n# randomized DAGs vs brute-force lexicographic reference\ndef brute(graph):\n    done, out = set(), []\n    while len(done) < len(graph):\n        ready = sorted(n for n, d in graph.items() if n not in done and all(x in done for x in d))\n        assert ready\n        done.add(ready[0]); out.append(ready[0])\n    return out\n\nrandom.seed(0)\nfor trial in range(500):\n    n = random.randint(0, 30)\n    names = random.sample(['n%02d' % i for i in range(30)], n)\n    g = {}\n    for i, name in enumerate(names):\n        # deps chosen from earlier names only => guaranteed DAG\n        k = random.randint(0, i)\n        g[name] = random.sample(names[:i], k)\n    assert schedule(g) == brute(g), g\n# random cyclic graphs: either valid topo order or ValueError, never hang\nfor trial in range(500):\n    n = random.randint(1, 12)\n    names = ['n%02d' % i for i in range(n)]\n    g = {x: random.sample(names, random.randint(0, 3)) for x in names}\n    try:\n        res = schedule(g)\n        assert sorted(res) == sorted(names)\n        pos = {x: i for i, x in enumerate(res)}\n        assert all(pos[d] < pos[x] for x, ds in g.items() for d in ds)\n    except ValueError:\n        pass\nprint('ALL_CHECKS_OK')\nEOF","description":"Run public test and comprehensive scheduler checks"}}]}}
